  "task": {
    "source_message_id": 543,
    "speaker": "client",
    "text": "My rough calculation gives a 140×100 board an area of 14000mm², with the components occupying about 5200mm², or ~37% coverage. That still seems comfortably within normal PCB density and should route cleanly on 8 layers.\n\nRather than consolidating everything into a 2x24+12p, I'd like to retain the individual JST connectors. The modular arrangement matters for the enclosure: every sensor gets its own clean cable, and the boards slide into rails. A single large connector feeding a fan-out ribbon cable would leave the enclosure wiring messy and difficult to service.\n\nBecause the components are already placed in KiCad, could you resize the outline to 140×100 and make a rough rearrangement? I am not proficient with KiCad, so what would take me hours should take you minutes with the complete project already open. I would really appreciate you trying the resize on your side.\n\nKeeping the ESP32 on the edge is fine."
  },
